ongowski</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Staudinger</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hofbauer</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Dufek</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Eder</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Raab</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Thell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schuster</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Frass</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of a conventional tracheal airway with the Combitube in an urban emergency medical services system run by physicians</article-title><source>Resuscitation</source><year>2003</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12668296</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0300-9572(02)00435-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koerner</surname><given-names>IP</given-names></name><name><surname>Brambrink</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fiberoptic techniques</article-title><source>Best Pract Res Clin Anaesthesiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>611</fpage><lpage>621</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16408537</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.bpa.2005.07.006</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>V&#x000e9;zina</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Tr&#x000e9;panier</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicole</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lessard</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Complications associated with the Esophageal-Tracheal Combitube in the pre-ho